  realised sigma(delta) = 0.7146   band-limited target ~ 1.2888
  [OK] realised variance within a factor 1.80 of a crude band-limited target -- adequate, and note EVERY result below is a RATIO to the global rms of the same field, so overall normalisation cancels exactly

====================================================================================================
S2. <|g| | delta> for the GAUSSIAN field -- testing the parity argument numerically
====================================================================================================
  global rms |g| (arb units) = 3.45059
           delta bin      cells   <|g|^2>^1/2  ratio to global
        -1.0 to -0.5    1140969       3.45035           0.9999
        -0.5 to +0.0    1826017       3.44956           0.9997
        +0.0 to +0.5    1825013       3.45064           1.0000
        +0.5 to +1.0    1141839       3.45090           1.0001
        +1.0 to +3.0     571600       3.45194           1.0004
       +3.0 to +10.0         87       3.61949           1.0489
  PARITY PREDICTION: for a Gaussian field <g_i delta> = 0, so the ratio should be ~1 in
  every bin, i.e. acceleration statistically INDEPENDENT of local density.
  [OK] every delta bin has |g| within 15-20% of the global rms (range 1.000-1.049) -- the parity argument is CONFIRMED numerically: no density dependence at Gaussian order

